## Dialogues
####################

dialogue.guia_sandra_0=Welcome to the Museo Goya, Colección Fundación Ibercaja. Museo Camón Aznar! This year, we have something very special: we are celebrating the 250th anniversary of Goya's self-portrait. To commemorate this occasion, we have prepared a unique exhibition about the Master Brush, the object believed to have been used by Goya to create his most iconic works. I'm so excited for you to see all of this in person - it's going to be a truly unforgettable experience!
dialogue.guia_sandra_1=I recommend exploring the entire museum. As you go along, you'll find other guides specialized in different sections who will share fascinating information about Goya. Feel free to approach them to learn more about the different stages of the artist's life. See you at the end of the tour!
dialogue.guia_sandra_1_b=I recommend exploring the entire museum. As you go along, you'll find other guides specialized in different sections who will share fascinating information about Goya. Feel free to approach them to learn more about the different stages of the artist's life. See you at the end of the tour!
dialogue.guia_joaquin=Welcome to the Museo Goya, Colección Fundación Ibercaja. Museo Camón Aznar! This year, we are celebrating the 250th anniversary of Goya's self-portrait. Don't miss the special exhibition of the Master Brush, an absolutely unique piece.
dialogue.guia_luis=Did you know that this building has changed a lot over the years? Before becoming what you see today, it was a drawing academy. These walls are filled with brushstrokes!
dialogue.guia_roberto=In the museum, we have a special selection of 48 works by Goya that showcase his evolution as an artist. From his portraits to his darkest paintings, each one has a story worth discovering. You can't miss them!
dialogue.guia_monica=Goya's engravings are pure satire, social criticism, and deep personal reflections. For example, in the engraving §oThe Sleep of Reason Produces Monsters§r, Goya wanted to express that when reason falls asleep, ghostly visions and hallucinations of monstrous beings emerging from the darkness appear. Interesting, right?
dialogue.visitante_01=I've traveled from very far to see this museum. Goya's work has something that goes beyond language, don't you think?
dialogue.visitante_02=This museum is more than just a place to admire art - it's a journey through the life of a genius. It's truly fascinating and captivating.
dialogue.visitante_03=The red room is dedicated to sculptures. Although I appreciate all kinds of art, I must admit that my true passion is painting.
dialogue.visitante_04=They say the Master Brush is the secret behind Goya's unique brushstrokes. Its history is surrounded by mystery, but it's fascinating to imagine it in his hands, isn't it?
dialogue.visitante_05=I like how this space gives you a moment to breathe between rooms. It feels like the museum is inviting you to reflect.
dialogue.visitante_06=This is just a hallway... How much farther until we reach the Black Paintings? I want to see something striking, something that makes me feel what Goya captured in those works.
dialogue.visitante_07=I remember seeing these paintings for the first time as a child. I didn't understand them, but something drew me in. Now I know it was Goya's intensity and passion - like his emotions had come to life in every brushstroke.
dialogue.visitante_08=These etchings are so detailed! They inspire me to experiment with new techniques in my own workshop.
dialogue.visitante_09=I had never seen an etching in person before. It's amazing how something so small can hold so much power.
dialogue.visitante_10=These works always leave an impression on me. It's as if Goya truly understood fear, loneliness... feelings we all experience but struggle to express.
dialogue.mecanico_0=These lights have to be just right. It's not just about illuminating; it's about framing Goya's works so they shine as they deserve.
dialogue.guia_pablo_0=Welcome to the "Master Brush" exhibition. Through this piece, we explore Goya's artistic process. But before we begin, I invite you to walk around this room and discover some of his most influential works. Don't forget to visit the adjacent rooms. When you're done, come back and talk to me.
dialogue.guia_pablo_1=It's a unique collector's piece! But before I tell you more about it, why not explore the other rooms in the museum? I wouldn't want you to miss anything we have to show you!
dialogue.guia_pablo_2=Alright, now let me tell you more about Goya's "Master Brush." It is believed that this brush was the tool he used to bring his first works to life. There are also stories about an easel with a blank canvas that may have been the surface where he used this brush, although its whereabouts remain a mystery...
dialogue.guia_pablo_3=Whoa! What just happened? This shouldn't be happening... Give me a moment, I'll talk to the technician to get it fixed.
dialogue.apagon_guias=We're checking what happened with the lights. The technician Antonio, who is at the exit of the Etchings Room, is already working on it. Could you see if he needs a hand?
dialogue.apagon_roberto=We're checking what happened with the lights. The technician Antonio, who is to my left at the exit of the Etchings Room, is already working on it. Could you see if he needs a hand?
dialogue.apagon_visitantes_01=Wow, first time I've ever been left in the dark in a museum! I just hope no painting falls on me.
dialogue.apagon_visitantes_02=Is this part of the experience? Because if it is, there was no warning at the entrance...
dialogue.apagon_visitantes_03=This is the last straw... I came to see art, not to play hide and seek!
dialogue.apagon_visitantes_04=This is very immersive, but I'd prefer a little light so I don't trip...
dialogue.apagon_visitantes_05=Blackout! Now all we need is someone to say this is a tribute to Goya's dark period.
dialogue.apagon_visitantes_06=Well, at least the ticket comes with a bit of mystery. Do you think we'll get a discount for this?
dialogue.apagon_visitantes_07=Blackout or artistic performance? I don't even know what to expect in a museum anymore.
dialogue.apagon_visitantes_08=Is it just me, or do the eyes in the paintings still seem to be watching us, even in the dark?
dialogue.apagon_visitantes_09=I was afraid of getting lost before, but now I think even the staff doesn't know where they are.
dialogue.apagon_visitantes_10=If the lights don't come back soon, I just hope someone has a good horror story to share.
dialogue.apagon_visitantes_11=And what if this is the brush's fault? Are we sure it doesn't have some weird powers?
dialogue.goya_quieto=Alright, I'll wait here. This place is so strange that I can hardly look away. Maybe, if I manage to remember everything, I'll capture it on a canvas...
dialogue.goya_seguir=Alright, I'll follow you. If this dream is to continue, I'd best not lose sight of where it's taking me.
dialogue.goya_00=Hello? Who's there?
dialogue.goya_01=What kind of sorcery is this? Tell me, who are you?
dialogue.goya_01_b=Who am I? I am Francisco de Goya! Just a moment ago, I was peacefully painting my self-portrait, and suddenly... I find myself here, with you. What kind of strange place is this?
dialogue.goya_02=A "museum" about §o"Goya"§r, you say? What a strange idea! But if the goal is for people to §osee§r my works, then why is this place in complete darkness?
dialogue.goya_03=So, you were visiting the museum, and suddenly the lights went out. How curious. But more importantly, how did I end up in this place?
dialogue.goya_05=You say I came out of my self-portrait? What a vivid dream I must be having! Wait... That brush in your hands... I recognize it. Where did you get it?
dialogue.goya_06=That is my Master Brush! I've had it since my youth, when I was just starting in art. But what is it doing here, and why do you have it? Alright... Keep it for now, until we figure out what's going -
dialogue.goya_07=Silence! Do you hear those whispers? I don't think we're alone... Who are those figures behind you? You should go and ask them - I'll wait here...
dialogue.goya_08_b=I don't think we're alone... Who are those figures behind you? You should go and ask them - I'll wait here...
dialogue.felix_01=What is this place? You there, tell me, what land is this? I've never seen anything like it in my explorations!
dialogue.luisa_01=What is going on? Where am I? What kind of court is this? Tell me, am I under some sort of spell?
dialogue.nina_01=Excuse me... where are my friends? Everything feels so strange... Are these things toys? And you, are you a wizard?
dialogue.goya_09=Wait... those figures. That's Félix de Azara, María Luisa de Parma, and that girl - they're all part of my paintings! That means... this isn't a dream? Is this really happening?!
dialogue.goya_09_b=This is unbelievable! If both they and I have "come out of my paintings," as you say, then perhaps other works have come to life as well... We must do something about it!
dialogue.goya_10=Do you want to help? Well then... We'll have to return all the characters to their respective paintings before chaos spreads. I'll go with you until we make sure everything is back to normal. What do you say?
dialogue.goya_11=Excellent! But how could we do that...?%1All of this started when you picked up my brush. That means we might be able to use it to help us...
dialogue.goya_12=Let's start with those three. They look lost, so I think the best thing would be to guide them back to their paintings in this room. But with this darkness, I doubt we'll be able to do anything...
dialogue.goya_13=What is that? The brush has started to glow! How is that possible? It looks like it's gained some sort of special power... Do you think we could use it to light the way to each painting?
dialogue.goya_14=The brush has just launched a glowing ball of paint! Well, given the situation, I suppose nothing surprises me anymore...
dialogue.goya_15=Alright, now it's all up to you. Talk to each of the characters from my paintings and use the brush to light the way to their respective artworks. I'll wait for you here.
dialogue.goya_15_b=Now it's all in your hands. Talk to each of the characters from my paintings and make sure they return to their respective artworks in each room. Use the brush to guide them with its light. I'll be waiting here.
dialogue.felix_02=I must admit, this place confuses me. I do not belong to this time or this place. Could you, by any chance, help me find a way to return to my era?
dialogue.luisa_02=You, kind stranger, it seems I do not belong to this place or your time. I beg you, in the name of your noble heart, could you help me return to my home?
dialogue.nina_02=Please, sir... I know this is not my place or my time. Everything here is far too strange. Would you help me find my way back home? I miss my friends... and I don't know how to return.
dialogue.felix_cuadro=It looks like Félix de Azara is back in his place. He might want to say something to you before you continue.
dialogue.luisa_cuadro=Has María Luisa de Parma returned to her place? She may have a few words for you before you move on.
dialogue.nina_cuadro=The girl is back where she belongs. You should talk to her before continuing.
dialogue.felix_05=Wonderful, my friend! This brush seems like a divine work. A thousand thanks for your help and kindness. Now, I shall return to my place, where I belong. May life reward you with the same good fortune. Farewell!
dialogue.luisa_05=Oh, how marvellous this brush is, guiding me back! I have no words to express my gratitude. Farewell, kind guide, and may fortune always be with you.
dialogue.nina_05=Thank you, sir... This glowing path has led me home. I will never forget your kindness. Goodbye... and always take care of the magic.
dialogue.goya_16=I am deeply grateful that you have returned these characters to their places, but I suspect we are not done fixing the chaos in the museum. I can still feel something dark lingering here. We must investigate further. Lead the way.
dialogue.goya_16_a=I suspect we are not done fixing the chaos in the museum. I can still feel something dark lingering here. We must investigate further. Lead the way.
dialogue.mecanico_01=I'm working to fix this mess with the lighting, but I need your help. There's a fuse box on the wall next to me. If you can activate it, that should restore power to this section. Be careful when handling it!
dialogue.mecanico_02=What the...? What is that creature in the Etchings Room?! HELP!!
dialogue.goya_17=I knew it! That creature is one of my creations! It's a monster I sketched in an etching to represent our own shadows and fears. We must follow it and find a way to return it to its artwork!
dialogue.guia_pablo_4=What was all that?! A monster has escaped into the streets of Zaragoza! Where did it come from? Please, do something!
dialogue.guia_sandra_2=A horrible creature just rushed past me! It ran out through the museum doors!
dialogue.guia_joaquin_2=I saw something terrifying run toward the exit! I think it went into the streets - please, don't let it get any farther!
dialogue.guia_luis_2=Those noises... and then that thing! I don't know what's happening, but you need to catch it before it causes more havoc!
dialogue.guia_roberto_2=This is madness! First, the blackout, and now that thing! It ran outside - you have to follow it!
dialogue.guia_monica_2=Something terrible just escaped from the museum. It was as if it had come to life from the etchings! Please, stop it!
dialogue.visitante_01_b=What was that?! I've never seen anything so terrifying! It ran straight outside!
dialogue.visitante_08_b=This can't be real... It was like an etching had come to life!
dialogue.visitante_09_b=Did anyone else see that? It was terrifying - it ran out through the doors!
dialogue.visitante_10_b=First the blackout, and now this... That creature ran right past me!
dialogue.visitante_02_b=I didn't see anything, but everyone's talking about a monster. Is this some kind of joke?
dialogue.visitante_03_b=I don't know what that was, but I saw it from the hallway. It looked like something out of a strange dream!
dialogue.visitante_04_b=I think I saw something rush toward the entrance, but it was so fast I don't even know if it was real.
dialogue.visitante_05_b=It was so loud my heart nearly stopped! I don't know what it was, but it ran like a stampede.
dialogue.visitante_06_b=At first, I thought it was part of some exhibit, but when it dashed through the entrance, I knew something was off. That was terrifying!
dialogue.visitante_07_b=I jumped into a corner just to avoid getting trampled! This shouldn't be happening in a museum!
dialogue.goya_18=The creature has escaped from the museum! We have no idea what kind of chaos it might unleash beyond these walls. We must go after it immediately!
dialogue.goya_19=Oh! Is this Zaragoza? What a wonderful city! I'd love to stay and admire its beautiful architecture, but we have more important matters to attend to. Come on, let's talk to the people and ask if they saw the creature leave the museum.
dialogue.jose=The winged monster? It flew right over my head! It looked like something straight out of a horror story!
dialogue.jose_b=The winged monster? It flew right over my head! It looked like something straight out of a horror story!
dialogue.isabel=How could I not see it? That horrible beast scared us all! But it was so erratic that it crashed into that red building behind us... and painted it black!
dialogue.isabel_b=How could I not see it? That horrible beast scared us all! But it was so erratic that it crashed into that red building behind us... and painted it black!
dialogue.sara=Did anyone else see that? It was like a monstrous shadow running through the street! Also, wasn't that building red before?
dialogue.sara_b=Did anyone else see that? It was like a monstrous shadow running through the street! Also, wasn't that building red before?
dialogue.manuel=That creature ran out of the museum, crashed into the red building, and stained it black!
dialogue.manuel_b=That creature ran out of the museum, crashed into the red building, and stained it black!
dialogue.remedios=That was terrifying! I was at home when I heard the monster slam into the building! I ran downstairs and found this mess!
dialogue.remedios_b=That was terrifying! I was at home when I heard the monster slam into the building! I ran downstairs and found this mess!
dialogue.alejandro=How is something like this roaming free in Zaragoza? Crashing into the building wasn't enough - it kept flying down the main street at full speed!
dialogue.alejandro_b=How is something like this roaming free in Zaragoza? Crashing into the building wasn't enough - it kept flying down the main street at full speed!
dialogue.goya_19_b=So the monster passed through here, crashed into that red building, and spilled its ink all over it. That's why it looks blackened now and has lost its beauty...
dialogue.goya_19_c=This is all my fault. I brought this creature to life in my works, and now it's wreaking havoc on my beloved Zaragoza. We can't let this continue. We must restore colour to the city!
dialogue.goya_20=How can we do that? Hmm... I wonder if we could use the brush to absorb colours from our surroundings. That way, with a brush full of colours, maybe we could repaint the building...
dialogue.goya_20_b=The brush has changed again! It's turned a neutral gray, perfect for absorbing colours...%1I've got it! In the park behind us, I saw a flowerpot with some beautiful §cred flowers§r. What if we use the brush to absorb their colour?
dialogue.goya_21=Of course! The brush has taken on the red colour from the flowers. You remember how it could throw glowing paint in the museum, right? Maybe now it can launch red paint. Why don't you try painting the building with it? I'll wait here.
dialogue.goya_22=Magnificent! This brush and its colours don't just paint - they bring life back to the city. But a good brush must be well cared for. Let's clean it in the water bucket before the paint dries. That way, it will be ready for the next masterful stroke.
dialogue.goya_23=The brush is ready. People have told us the monster escaped down the main street. We must follow it and restore life to every building it has stained, just as we did with this one. If you need help, come and talk to me.
dialogue.goya_23_c=The flowers will give us the colours we need. To get secondary colours like orange, green, or purple, mix the primary ones: red, yellow, and blue. And don't forget to clean the brush in the water bucket after each use - this way, it will always be ready to bring life back to beautiful Zaragoza.
dialogue.andrea=It looked like one of those creatures from Goya's etchings! But... it was real!
dialogue.vicente=I've never seen anything like that. It ran like the wind and had a truly terrifying shape!
dialogue.marcos=Look at that! It's leaving black marks everywhere it goes! What is that thing?
dialogue.elena=Is no one really going to do anything? That building is completely stained!
dialogue.luisa=This place never stops - there's always something to fix.
dialogue.mario=Sometimes it's tough, but this neighborhood has its own magic. Between the renovations and the people passing by, there's always something interesting to see.
dialogue.jaime=There are always people watching here, but we have to keep moving.
dialogue.fernando=The city is changing, but this little corner remains the same. It's like time doesn't pass here.
dialogue.daniela=I like walking through here after work. The atmosphere changes depending on the time of day, as if the neighborhood had different faces.
dialogue.carlos=Look at those black stains! That monster is ruining the beauty of our city!
dialogue.victoria=Will anyone be able to bring colour back to our city? This is a nightmare!
dialogue.marta=That's the strangest thing I've ever seen in Zaragoza! What was that?
dialogue.borja=It's leaving marks all over the walls! How are we supposed to clean that up?
dialogue.cristina=I can't believe what I just saw! It looked like a beast straight out of an old painting.
dialogue.raul=Was that some kind of trick from the museum? Because if it wasn't, someone should be worried.
dialogue.gonzalo=They say something strange came out of the museum, but I haven't seen anything around here. Could it be true?
dialogue.mariano=Look at what it did to that building's façade! It used to be so beautiful...
dialogue.antonia=Somebody help us! Every second that passes, more of our history disappears under those stains!
dialogue.emilio=Someone call the heritage authorities! This is a cultural disaster!
dialogue.leandro=I never thought I'd see something like this... Is that creature the cause of all this chaos in the city? But now it looks so defenseless.
dialogue.patricia=So this is the creature that caused all the chaos? I never imagined it would end up trapped in its own mess.
dialogue.lorena=Someone left their bucket of water here and ran away as soon as they saw the flying creature. It doesn't seem evil to me. If anything, it looks scared.
dialogue.carmen=I saw it. It was full of colours... as if it had absorbed everything it touched. It's strange, almost... tragic.
dialogue.alberto_0=I don't understand anything that's happening today...
dialogue.goya_24_0=Magnificent! Zaragoza shines once again in all its splendor. But... wait a moment, what is that in Plaza del Pilar? It looks like the monster... but it seems different, weaker. Let's get closer and find out what happened.
dialogue.goya_24_1=Look at it... It's on the ground, covered in colours, barely able to move. This monster is nothing more than a reflection of my own fears. It didn't escape the museum out of malice - it ran because it was afraid. It fears us more than we fear it.
dialogue.goya_24_3=If we help it regain its original form, I might be able to persuade it to return to its etching. For that, we need black ink.
dialogue.goya_24_4=Look at those black roses. Load their pigment into the brush and restore the monster's original darkness. Paint it just like you did with the buildings. I will speak to it afterward.
dialogue.goya_24_5=Listen, creature! We are not your enemies! I brought you to life as the embodiment of my fears, but you do not need to be afraid! Return to your original place, and there you shall find peace!
dialogue.goya_24_6=We've done it! The city shines once more, and the monster has returned to its place. Perhaps this is the end of -
dialogue.alberto_a=Hey! You two over there! Come quickly!
dialogue.goya_24_7=It looks like that boy wants to tell us something. Let's go talk to him.
dialogue.alberto=I ran out of the Basilica... There's something inside that shouldn't be possible. Figures that look like they've come straight out of the frescoes. If anyone can do something, it's you. Please, go inside and fix this!
dialogue.alberto_b=I ran out of the Basilica... There's something inside that shouldn't be possible. Figures that look like they've come straight out of the frescoes. If anyone can do something, it's you. Please, go inside and fix this!
dialogue.goya_24=That can't be a coincidence... There's a painting of mine inside the Basilica! If those figures have come to life, we must find out what's happening. Come, there's no time to lose!
dialogue.goya_24_b=This place brings back beautiful memories... Though now it feels different, as if tragedy has left its mark here. However, the aura remains the same. But we must not get distracted. Come, let's talk to that person to find out what happened here.
dialogue.goya_24_c=This place brings back beautiful memories... Though now it feels different, as if tragedy has left its mark here. However, the aura remains the same. But we must not get distracted. Come, let's talk to that person to find out what happened here.
dialogue.sacerdote_0=I was doing maintenance work at the Basilica when these strangely dressed people suddenly appeared. I don't understand anything...
dialogue.sacerdote_01=Something very strange just happened. Figures emerged from the fresco while I was working. One of them, who calls himself the Leader, seems to be in charge. You should talk to him. I'll stay here and keep an eye on things. Ask me if you need anything.
dialogue.sacerdote_01_b=Something very strange just happened. Figures emerged from the fresco while I was working. One of them, who calls himself the Leader, seems to be in charge. You should talk to him. I'll stay here and keep an eye on things. Ask me if you need anything.
dialogue.goya_25=I feared it... The figures from my fresco §oThe Adoration of the Name of God§r have come to life. And those clouds look exactly like the ones in my work. You must speak with the Leader to restore order. But how will you reach him? If the brush could recreate the strokes that formed those clouds, we might find a way...
dialogue.goya_26=Look at the brush! It has changed shape again! Why is it that every time I...? Never mind. Look toward the Leader, use the brush, and let's see how it surprises us this time.
dialogue.goya_26_b=Look at the brush! It has changed shape again! Why is it that every time I...? Never mind. Look toward the Leader, use the brush, and let's see how it surprises us this time.
dialogue.goya_26_c=The brush can now create floating clouds! Exactly what we need to reach him. Curious, isn't it? But be careful, they seem to vanish quickly, so you'll have to move fast. I trust you to fix this chaos. I'll wait for you here.
dialogue.goya_26_e=The brush can create floating clouds to help you reach distant places. If needed, you can dispel them by striking them with the brush, though they will also vanish on their own over time. Don't fear falling from great heights - the brush's aura will protect you from harm.
dialogue.angel_ezequiel=Something is wrong. My essence is out of place, but I don't know how to fix it... There is a void within me, but I am not the one who should guide you now...
dialogue.angel_ezequiel_01=I can't believe it! My companions and I were pulled from the fresco and became trapped here. Without their symbolic objects, they lost the way back and cannot return to the artwork. I have recovered mine, but the others still need help.
dialogue.angel_ezequiel_01_b=You arrived just in time. In this place, three companions are waiting for your help. Each has lost an essential object that allows them to return to the fresco they belong to. Speak with them and recover what they have lost so balance can be restored.
dialogue.angel_ezequiel_03=Your creative tool can generate floating clouds. Use it to reach my companions' objects and return them. With them, they will be able to return to the fresco they belong to. Do not fear the heights, the brush's power will protect you. When you are done, come back to me.
dialogue.angel_ezequiel_03_b=My companions need your help. They have lost the objects that allow them to return to the fresco they come from. Use your brush to create clouds and reach the high places where their belongings are. Do not fear the heights, the brush's power will protect you if you fall.
dialogue.angel_ezequiel_03_c=The brush can create floating clouds to help you reach distant places. If needed, you can dispel them by striking them with the brush, though they will also vanish on their own over time. Do not fear the heights, the brush's power will protect you if you fall.
dialogue.angel_idle=I'm sorry, I can't talk to you right now. I'm looking for a lost item. If you need anything, speak to our Leader.
dialogue.angel_musico_01=My harp's so close... but without it, I can't return to the fresco. It's on top of the central statue of the chapel. If you bring it to me, I'll be able to return to my place. Tell me when you're ready, and I'll help you reach the cloud above us so you can get it.
dialogue.angel_musico_01_b=My harp's so close... but without it, I can't return to the fresco. It's on top of the central statue of the chapel. If you bring it to me, I'll be able to return to my place. Tell me when you're ready, and I'll help you reach the cloud above us so you can get it.
dialogue.angel_explorador_01=My ancient scroll... without it, I can't return to the fresco. It's next to one of the pillars, visible from the cloud above us. When you're ready, tell me, and I'll take you to the cloud so you can reach it.
dialogue.angel_explorador_01_b=My ancient scroll... without it, I can't return to the fresco. It's next to one of the pillars, visible from the cloud above us. When you're ready, tell me, and I'll take you to the cloud so you can reach it.
dialogue.angel_gloton_01=Ah, my bunch of grapes... it may seem simple, but without it, I can't return to the fresco. It's on top of a lamp near the entrance. Let me know when you're ready, and I'll take you to the cloud above us so you can collect it.
dialogue.angel_gloton_01_b=Ah, my bunch of grapes... it may seem simple, but without it, I can't return to the fresco. It's on top of a lamp near the entrance. Let me know when you're ready, and I'll take you to the cloud above us so you can collect it.
dialogue.angel_musico_02=My harp! Thank you, now I can return to the fresco and continue the melody I left unfinished. Your help fit perfectly, like a note at the right moment. I won't forget this.
dialogue.angel_explorador_02=The scroll! My guide and reference... Thanks to you, I can resume my path and return to the fresco. You've restored the meaning of my search. Thank you.
dialogue.angel_gloton_02=Ah, my grapes! With them, I recover the drive I was missing to return to the fresco. I can't thank you enough, you've brought flavor back to my existence. A pity we can't share them...
dialogue.angel_ezequiel_04=Thank you for helping my companions and restoring what was lost. You've done far more than I expected. Now it's time for me to return as well, the fresco is complete again. May your path continue with the same determination. Farewell.
dialogue.sacerdote_03=Well... looks like everything's back to normal. The figures are in the fresco again, and nothing seems out of place anymore. Thanks for the help, really.
dialogue.goya_27=The figures have returned to the fresco, but all this has left me uneasy. The brush that helps us, the museum characters, the creature from the engraving, and now these figures... Why is all of this happening to us? Could there be a hidden meaning behind it all?
dialogue.goya_27_b=I know what we must do to find the answer - we must return to my origins, to the place where my journey began. We have to go to Fuendetodos, the land where I was born.
dialogue.goya_27_c=Yes, Fuendetodos - the place of my birth. It is more than just my homeland; it is the beginning of everything. If all of this has meaning, I am certain we will find it there. Let's go - I feel this will be our final destination.
dialogue.goya_28=Fuendetodos... this is where it all began. This place holds the first breaths of my life, the very foundations of who I am. After everything we've been through, I feel that the answers we seek are here.
dialogue.goya_28_b=Let's talk to the people of the village - perhaps their words will awaken something in my memory that can help us. Once you've spoken to them, we must enter my house. I'm certain that within its walls, we will uncover the mystery behind everything that's happening.
dialogue.goya_28_c=Let's talk to the people of the village - perhaps their words will awaken something in my memory that can help us. Once you've spoken to them, we must enter my house. I'm certain that within its walls, we will uncover the mystery behind everything that's happening.
dialogue.camila=Did you know that you're in the very village where Goya was born? This is where his journey began - one that would change the history of art. If you want to understand more about his life and legacy, this is the perfect place. Talk to Tomás, up the stairs, or Nancy, right here in front. They can tell you more about Francisco de Goya.
dialogue.camila_0=Did you know that you're in the very village where Goya was born? This is where his journey began - one that would change the history of art. If you want to understand more about his life and legacy, this is the perfect place. Talk to Tomás, up the stairs, or Nancy, right here in front. They can tell you more about Francisco de Goya.
dialogue.camila_b=Did you know that you're in the very village where Goya was born? This is where his journey began - one that would change the history of art. If you want to understand more about his life and legacy, this is the perfect place. Talk to Tomás, up the stairs, or Nancy, right here in front. They can tell you more about Francisco de Goya.
dialogue.goya_fuendetodos=The village where Goya was born? How strange it is to hear that in the third person while standing here myself! It's true - this was my beginning, but I never imagined that one day it would be seen as such an important part of my story.
dialogue.tomas=Did you know that Goya signed his works in many different ways? Sometimes he used just his last name, other times he added "de Goya," or even "Francisco de Goya." Each signature has its own story and reflects his evolution as an artist. By the way, have you spoken to Nancy at the entrance of Goya's Birthplace?
dialogue.tomas_0=Did you know that Goya signed his works in many different ways? Sometimes he used just his last name, other times he added "de Goya," or even "Francisco de Goya." Each signature has its own story and reflects his evolution as an artist. By the way, have you spoken to Nancy at the entrance of Goya's Birthplace?
dialogue.tomas_b=Did you know that Goya signed his works in many different ways? Sometimes he used just his last name, other times he added "de Goya," or even "Francisco de Goya." Each signature has its own story and reflects his evolution as an artist. By the way, have you spoken to Nancy at the entrance of Goya's Birthplace?
dialogue.goya_firmas=Different signatures? Bah! Sometimes I just got tired of writing it all out. But seeing how well-known I am now, maybe I should have signed more clearly to avoid confusion...
dialogue.nancy=This is the Casa Natal de Goya, the house where he was born in 1746. A humble home, but full of history. If you'd like to visit, it's open to the public, and my colleague Tomás, who's up the stairs, can tell you all about Goya's signatures. By the way, your companion... looks like he showed up in full Goya cosplay!
dialogue.nancy_0=This is the Casa Natal de Goya, the house where he was born in 1746. A humble home, but full of history. If you'd like to visit, it's open to the public, and my colleague Tomás, who's up the stairs, can tell you all about Goya's signatures. By the way, your companion... looks like he showed up in full Goya cosplay!
dialogue.nancy_b=This is the Casa Natal de Goya, the house where he was born in 1746. A humble home, but full of history. If you'd like to visit, it's open to the public, and my colleague Tomás, who's up the stairs, can tell you all about Goya's signatures. By the way, your companion... looks like he showed up in full Goya cosplay!
dialogue.goya_casa=My house... how it fills my heart to see it still standing! This is where it all began - my first dreams, my first struggles. It is an honor that it is now a place where others can learn about my origins.
dialogue.goya_29=This house... so familiar, yet so distant. This is where the days that shaped the artist I became first began. That brush you carry - the same one I held in my early years - seems to be the key to everything. I am certain that the answers lie here, in the place where my journey started.
dialogue.goya_30=To understand what is happening, I need to recover my memories. Something essential about me is still missing. There must be objects in this house that will help me regain fragments of my memory. If we find them, we can complete this puzzle and uncover the truth.
dialogue.goya_31=For example, look at that small wooden figurine on the table... I feel like it is connected to something important from my past, though I can't quite remember what. If I could recover that lost memory, I would understand how it influenced my life as an artist. Perhaps the brush can help us reveal its meaning.
dialogue.goya_32=The brush has changed again! Of course, now I see it! From the moment you picked it up in the museum, it has always responded to our needs. It lit our way in the darkness, restored Zaragoza with its colours, and created clouds to help the figures in the Basilica. It seems to be connected to our desires, guiding us every step of the way...
dialogue.goya_33=Surely, all of this has been possible because you have been the link. You are the one who has wielded the brush, and through it, you have given form to our wishes. Perhaps now it can do the same with my memories, don't you think? Let's try it on the figurine - maybe it will reveal a part of me that I have forgotten.
dialogue.goya_35_b=Use the brush on the figurine. If it truly reacts to our desires as I believe, you might be able to capture part of my lost memory from it. This is something we need to understand my past and my legacy.
dialogue.goya_36=Do you see it? Now the brush is charged with one of my memories. It's time to use it! Step back a little and throw the memory to me. Don't worry, you won't hurt me.
dialogue.goya_estatua=This figurine... I once held one just like it in my hands. It was my practice companion in my early attempts to bring life to paper. I was obsessed with capturing every detail of the human form. That object, along with the brush, was a key part of my learning process as an artist.
dialogue.goya_38=Now you hold the power to recover my memories. That figurine was just the beginning. Let's explore the house and look for objects that have reacted to the presence of the brush. Each one holds a fragment of my past, of what shaped me as an artist, and will help us uncover why we are here. Let's go!
dialogue.goya_memorias=You have the power to recover my memories in your hands. Search the house for objects that respond to the brush. Then, use it on them to capture the memory fragment and throw it to me. This way, I will remember their significance and discover what has brought us here.
dialogue.goya_memorias_on=Come on, step back a little and throw that memory to me. I'll stay still. I need to recover it to understand the path that shaped me and uncover why I am here today.
dialogue.goya_leche=This pitcher... There was one just like it in my home. I would spend hours watching how the light played on its surface, creating reflections and shadows that seemed to dance with one another. It was through objects like this that I learned to understand the contrasts I later captured with my brush.
dialogue.goya_cofre=This chest... It looks just like the one I had in my childhood. My parents kept my earliest drawings inside - small sketches from a young dreamer. Inside it was also the very brush you now hold in your hands.
dialogue.goya_cama=This bed... It's similar to the one I had as a child. I spent nights dreaming of human, celestial, and demonic figures. Here is where the characters I later painted with the brush you carry were born.
dialogue.goya_39=Now I understand everything! These memories haven't just restored my past - they have returned my very essence, my "colour." Everything has led us to this moment because here, in this house, lies an object of great importance.
dialogue.goya_40=It all began when you picked up the brush and I appeared. Now I know that I emerged from my painting because we were meant to come here together. You see, the Master Brush has guided us to its other half, the missing piece of this puzzle - my precious Master Easel.
dialogue.goya_41=The brush and the easel were my companions at the start of my journey. The brush stayed with me until I lost it during a trip, and it seems it eventually ended up in that museum. But when I moved to Madrid, I couldn't take my first easel with me, and I never knew what became of it. Now I have no doubt - the easel is here, in this house.
dialogue.goya_42=But... where? My family always spoke of a special room in this house, one with a doorway painted pink. The easel must be inside! Let's search for it.
dialogue.goya_43=This is the place... I can feel it. Behind this pink door lies my Master Easel. We need to find a way to get through.
dialogue.goya_43_b=Of course... The brush is offering its final help. Go on, launch a projectile at the pink wood. I'm sure that will clear our path.
dialogue.goya_44=Now we can move forward. Come, let's go together. It's time to return everything to where it belongs.
dialogue.goya_45=There it is - my first easel, the inseparable companion of this brush. Together, they marked the beginning of my artistic journey, the very foundations of my legacy. But my time has passed - now it is your turn. These tools will allow you to leave your own mark on Zaragoza.
dialogue.goya_46=Place the brush on the easel, where it has always belonged. They were the origin of my dreams, and now they are destined to mark the beginning of yours.
dialogue.goya_47=At last... the brush and the easel are together again, after so much time. Thanks to you, I have not only recovered my history but also found someone with the strength and vision to continue what this brush once began. Now, the path is yours.
dialogue.goya_48=Of course! It was no coincidence that the brush responded every time we needed it. Everything led you here, to this very moment. Now, the power to create is in your hands. It is your turn to leave your mark on Zaragoza and build a legacy that transcends time, just as mine did.
dialogue.goya_49=Come on! Use the easel. It will take us to the place that belongs to you - your own blank canvas. There, you will have the space to unleash your creativity. I will be by your side for this final stage. I'll see you there.
dialogue.goya_final=Would you like to return to the construction zone, or would you prefer to stay here a little longer?
dialogue.goya_construccion=This space is your "blank canvas", just as it was mine at the start of my journey. Choose a historical or artistic landmark of Zaragoza that inspires you and recreate its essence here. You will honor our history and begin your own legacy.
dialogue.goya_construccion_2=Let's get to work! Choose a historical or artistic landmark of Zaragoza that inspires you and bring its essence to life here. If you need guidance or wish to return to any of the areas we explored, talk to me, or close this text with the cross to begin. This is your moment to bring your vision to life and build your legacy!

