sign.cartel_museo_bienvenida.title=§lWelcome to the Goya Museum§r%1%1Step into the world of Francisco de Goya, master of painting and etching. This museum invites you to discover his life and legacy, from his early days in Aragón to the works that revolutionized universal art. %1%1Explore the complete series of his etchings, witnesses to his critical and modern vision, and visit our special commemorative exhibition for the 250th anniversary of Goya's Self-Portrait - a key work in his career and a reflection of his genius.
sign.cartel_museo_contemporaneos.title=§lGoya and His Contemporaries§r %1%1The Goya Museum presents not only the work of Francisco de Goya but also that of artists who shaped his path. The brothers Francisco and Ramón Bayeu, Goya's brothers-in-law and collaborators, worked with him on key projects, and their influence was crucial to his artistic development. %1%1Corrado Giaquinto and Anton Rafael Mengs, masters of Rococo and Neoclassicism, laid the foundations for an artistic renewal that deeply impacted Goya. These works illustrate how the styles of the time contributed to the evolution of one of the greatest geniuses of painting. 
sign.cartel_museo_ninos.title=§l"Kids Games" Series§r %1%1This room houses part of the "Kids Games" series by Francisco de Goya. %1%1The series features scenes of children, ranging from 2 to 13 years old, in action and movement, inspired by Goya's childhood memories in Zaragoza. In these works, he depicts them playing, jumping, fighting, or bullfighting, dressed in costumes that mimic soldiers' uniforms, wearing paper hats, or using makeshift weapons made of reeds. 
