sign.cartel_zaragoza_1.title=§eAttention!§r In the streets of the city, you will find an open-air exhibition called §eThe History of Zaragoza§r%1with signs full of interesting facts.%1Read them to discover Zaragoza!
sign.cartel_zaragoza_2.title=Zaragoza has more than §e2,000 years of history§r, shaped by different civilizations such as the Iberians, Romans, Andalusi cultures, and medieval kingdoms. It is also known as §ethe city of four cultures.§r
sign.cartel_zaragoza_3.title=The §eParque Grande José Antonio Labordeta§r is one of the largest parks in Spain, covering more than 400,000 square meters.
sign.cartel_zaragoza_4.title=The §efirst film ever shot in Spain§r was "Salida de misa de doce del Pilar de Zaragoza", and as you can imagine from the title, it was filmed in Zaragoza in 1897.
sign.cartel_zaragoza_5.title=The §ePalace of Aljafería§r is the northernmost palace of its kind in Europe, as well as one of the most luxurious and best-preserved from the Taifa period.
sign.cartel_zaragoza_6.title=Zaragoza is the only city in the world with two active and independent cathedrals: §eEl Pilar and La Seo§r. They are just 150 metres apart.
sign.cartel_zaragoza_7.title=Beneath the city, there are archaeological remains from different eras, such as the §eRoman forum, the public baths, and the river port§r. You can visit them and travel back in time.
sign.cartel_basilica_1.title=The §ecentral dome§r of this Basilica, one of the largest in Spain, is decorated with a monumental fresco that was also designed by Goya.
sign.cartel_basilica_2.title=During the Spanish Civil War, the §eBasilica of El Pilar§r was bombed, but none of the bombs exploded. Two of them are preserved as a testament to this unusual event.
sign.cartel_basilica_3.title=§eLook up!§r  %1There you will find the fresco by Goya "The Adoration of the Name of God". Painted in 1772, it is one of the artist's first major projects.
sign.cartel_basilica_4.title=The §eBasilica of El Pilar§r has eleven domes and four towers. The central dome acts as the visual axis of the building and organizes the interior space, uniting architecture, painting, and light.
sign.cartel_fuendetodos_1.title=In Fuendetodos, several §esnow pits or ice wells§r are preserved-historic structures where snow was stored to be used for food preservation or as a medical remedy.
sign.cartel_fuendetodos_2.title=In the surroundings of Fuendetodos, you can find §edry stone corrals§r, traditional structures used by shepherds to shelter their livestock.
sign.cartel_fuendetodos_3.title=Fuendetodos was founded in the 14th century during the §eReconquista§r, and its original name, §eFuent de Todos§r, referred to a spring that supplied water to its first settlers.
sign.cartel_construccion_1.title=§l§eConstruction area: create your legacy in Zaragoza§r%1%1§fThe Master Brush has brought you to this space, a place without limits where something new can begin.%1%1Your challenge is to §abuild a creation inspired by Zaragoza's historical or artistic heritage§r, using as a starting point whatever impacted you most during the journey.%1%1This is your blank canvas: your own mark begins here.
sign.cartel_construccion_2.title=§l§eInstructions:§r%1%1- Choose a historical or artistic heritage element from Zaragoza that inspires you%1- Recreate its essence: it can be a building, a scene, a detail, or a free reinterpretation%1- Decide what aspect you want to highlight: shape, atmosphere, history, or meaning%1- Let your creativity flow and build your own legacy%1%1§7§oIf you need guidance or want to return to a previous area, talk to Goya.

